From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0791: pipeline storage report: what the preload did with every stored description and how many run-time pipelines were transfer ones ('[pipeline-storage]', extended '[pipelines]')

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (pipeline-cache diagnosis of 2026-11-27, scratch/pipeline-cache/DIAGNOSIS.md, question 3)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Diagnostics for the pipeline storage; no behaviour change. The preload used to skip stored descriptions silently (vertex or
  pixel shader missing, translation missing or invalid, no root signature, already known) and reported only what it queued. It now logs
  one '[pipeline-storage]' line with the number of descriptions and shaders in the files, how many became pipelines, and each skip
  reason; the hashes of the skipped descriptions are kept, so the 10 s '[pipelines]' line can say how many of the run-time creations
  were draws whose description the file already held. New data exports rexgpu_transfer_pipeline_creations and
  rexgpu_transfer_pipeline_us (the part of rexgpu_pipeline_creations that is render target transfer pipelines, and the time spent
  making them), and the '[pipelines]' line splits the counter into render target transfer (with ms), new draw descriptions and stored
  ones. Applies on top of 0790 (the transfer counter sits in the code 0790 touches).
  Validated 2026-11-27 (runs b-a1, b-b1..b-b3): 'preloaded 925 (driver creation failed 0), skipped 0 ...' and '[pipelines] 120 created
  (120 render target transfer in 17 ms; 0 for draws: 0 new in the storage, 0 already stored but skipped at the preload)'. The
  negative test (skipped counts with a missing shader file) was not run.
Bucket: REDO

0791-pipeline-storage-report.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, T0/T2).

